{"step_index":5,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T14:22:14Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nSubjective Examination: Demographic Data. Chief complaint, History of Present illness including functional limitation, Past Medical Surgical history, Family history, Occupational & Personal history, Socio-Economic, Environmental and Psychological History, Drug and Treatment History///// musculoskeletal —-Vital Parameters\r\n Temperature: State route used (axillary/oral) and presence of fever.\r\n Normal Value: 98.6°F (37°C) (Range: 97.8°F – 99.1°F / 36.5°C – 37.3°C)\r\n Respiratory Rate (RR): Count rate, rhythm, depth, and pattern (thoraco-abdominal in females, abdomino-thoracic in males).\r\n Normal Value: 12–20 breaths/min, regular, quiet, and unlabored.\r\n Peripheral Pulses: Palpate radial, dorsalis pedis, or posterior tibial; document rate, rhythm, volume, and bilateral symmetry.\r\n Normal Value: 60–100 beats/min, regular, Grade 2+ (normal, palpable bilaterally).\r\n Blood Pressure (BP): Record systolic/diastolic pressure, patient position (sitting/supine), and arm used.\r\n Normal Value: <120/80 mmHg (Systolic: 100–120 mmHg, Diastolic: 60–80 mmHg).\r\nGeneral Musculoskeletal Observations\r\n Body Built: Document somatotype (ectomorphic, mesomorphic, endomorphic) and calculated BMI.\r\n Normal Finding: Mesomorphic build; BMI 18.5–24.9 kg/m².\r\n Attitude of Limb: Note resting spatial position of the limb relative to anatomical neutral (e.g., antalgic posturing, guarding).\r\n Normal Finding: Symmetrical, resting comfortably in anatomical neutral without protective spasm.\r\n Bony Contours: Inspect continuity, prominence, and bilateral symmetry of standard bony landmarks.\r\n Normal Finding: Intact, smooth, and symmetrical, without step-offs, spurs, or abnormal prominence.\r\n Deformities: Identify structural (fixed) vs. postural (flexible) deformities, plane of deviation, and joint involved.\r\n Normal Finding: Absent; normal physiological axial and appendicular alignment.\r\n Trophic Changes: Assess skin texture, shine, hair loss, nail changes, pigmentation, or signs of autonomic dysfunction.\r\n Normal Fi\n<truncated 18748 bytes>\ning tape used across three levels, measuring the difference from maximal expiration to maximal inspiration:\r\n Axillary Level: 2nd–3rd intercostal space.\r\n Mammary / Nipple Level: 4th intercostal space.\r\n Xiphisternal Level: 8th–10th rib margin / xiphisternal junction.\r\n Normal Value: 3\\text{--}5\\text{ cm} (1.5\\text{--}2\\text{ inches}) difference between full expiration and full inspiration across all levels.\r\n Symmetry of Chest Movement:\r\n Method: Examiner places hands firmly on anterior/posterior chest wall with thumbs pinching a midline skin fold at the upper lobes (clavicular region), middle lobes (axillary/nipple), and lower lobes (10th ribs).\r\n Normal Value: Bilateral, symmetrical, and simultaneous excursion; thumbs diverge equally from the midline by \\sim 2\\text{ cm} on each side during deep inspiration.\r\nAnthropometric Measurements\r\n Body Mass Index (BMI):\r\n Formula: \\text{Weight (kg)} / [\\text{Height (m)}]^2\r\n Classifications (WHO):\r\n Underweight: <18.5\\text{ kg/m}^2\r\n Normal: 18.5\\text{--}24.9\\text{ kg/m}^2\r\n Overweight: 25.0\\text{--}29.9\\text{ kg/m}^2\r\n Obese: \\ge 30.0\\text{ kg/m}^2 (Asian cut-off for obesity: \\ge 25.0\\text{ kg/m}^2)\r\n Waist-to-Hip Ratio (WHR):\r\n Method: Waist measured at the narrowest circumference between the lower rib margin and iliac crest (umbilicus level); Hip measured at the widest horizontal circumference over the buttocks/greater trochanters.\r\n Formula: \\text{Waist Circumference} / \\text{Hip Circumference}\r\n Normal Values (Low Cardiovascular / Metabolic Risk):\r\n Males: <0.90 (Central obesity: \\ge 0.90)\r\n Females: <0.85 (Central obesity: \\ge 0.85)\r\n////////\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-17T19:52:14+05:30.\n</ADD